\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Square-integrable functions beyond one mode}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{\ref{fdip-004J} keeps one frequency fixed while the
[circle mesh](fdip-004H) grows. The interpolation #{I_n} turns
the sampled mode into a function on the circle, and that
function approaches the corresponding continuum mode. A
square-integrable function has infinitely many frequencies.
Each spacing of the mesh also determines an average of the
function. Applied to those averages, does the mesh resolvent,
once interpolated, approach the continuum resolvent?}
